                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.154A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-27T17:00:00+03:00">June 27, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 1—12:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>837. Department’s mail instruction 510, November 15, 1940. The Legation is in
                    receipt of a note, dated April 10, from the Saudi Arabian Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs conveying King Ibn Saud’s appreciation of the offer of the American
                    Government to cooperate in obtaining the services of American road engineers but
                    stating that the Saudi Arabian Government deems it advisable to hold the matter
                    in abeyance for the duration of the present international crisis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
